1
00:00:00,891 --> 00:00:07,121
Okay, folks, now I'll show you what the oscillogram actually looks like — the one you all want to see.

2
00:00:07,281 --> 00:00:12,001
So, this is the coil, we hook up to it.

3
00:00:13,761 --> 00:00:17,721
Frequency 67.53, where this effect is observed.

4
00:00:18,181 --> 00:00:25,681
And the duty cycle we get — let me tell you exactly — the duty cycle is just 1%.

5
00:00:26,521 --> 00:00:29,741
So, we apply it, and what do we see?

6
00:00:29,961 --> 00:00:30,761
Here's what we see.

7
00:00:31,381 --> 00:00:33,601
So, this is it right here.

8
00:00:34,241 --> 00:00:36,841
This isn't ferroresonance, this is magnetostriction.

9
00:00:37,801 --> 00:00:42,661
I don't get why Roma called this ferroresonance.

10
00:00:43,601 --> 00:00:44,581
This is how it works.

11
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:47,121
A lot of people have shown you this.

12
00:00:47,961 --> 00:00:52,341
So, the ferrite ramps up, dips down, and then smoothly ramps up again.

13
00:00:52,341 --> 00:00:54,881
This is what the oscillogram is supposed to look like.

14
00:00:55,321 --> 00:00:56,761
Something like that, let's say.

15
00:00:56,981 --> 00:01:01,661
And by the way, the drive frequency doesn't quite match.

16
00:01:01,741 --> 00:01:02,021
Well, whatever.

17
00:01:02,861 --> 00:01:08,541
The main thing, I'll say it again, is the operating principle...

18
00:01:08,541 --> 00:01:12,681
And now if I start increasing the duty cycle, watch what happens.

19
00:01:14,881 --> 00:01:15,401
See?

20
00:01:15,921 --> 00:01:18,001
But you shouldn't overdo it.

21
00:01:18,001 --> 00:01:24,661
This collapse that starts from the top — that's not good.

22
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:26,881
That means the current starts clamping down on the transistor.

23
00:01:29,961 --> 00:01:31,361
You shouldn't push it that far.

24
00:01:32,841 --> 00:01:37,021
So you need to watch it on the sweep.

25
00:01:37,101 --> 00:01:42,161
Here the transistor turns on, and as soon as it turns off, the ferrite starts working.

26
00:01:42,941 --> 00:01:43,761
That's all there is to it.

27
00:01:43,901 --> 00:01:49,501
So you need to do everything you can to keep this generator from guzzling current.

28
00:01:49,881 --> 00:01:54,061
Because you're not going to get much out of this ferrite.

29
00:01:54,801 --> 00:01:55,321
Right.

30
00:01:55,661 --> 00:01:57,781
Which is why the transistor here is the type it is.

31
00:01:58,381 --> 00:01:58,901
That's one.

32
00:01:59,361 --> 00:01:59,881
Second.

33
00:02:00,561 --> 00:02:04,081
So, this whole circuit here, it guzzles current too.

34
00:02:04,321 --> 00:02:06,361
Because we need it at 12 volts.

35
00:02:06,401 --> 00:02:08,701
I built this to light things up at 12 volts.

36
00:02:08,701 --> 00:02:11,901
You see, I needed to light the flashlight at 12 volts.

37
00:02:12,581 --> 00:02:15,161
Damn, why would I want 3 volts and all that.

38
00:02:15,581 --> 00:02:18,781
I could've just taken the energy straight from here.

39
00:02:19,341 --> 00:02:22,481
You get 6-7 volts here from this coil.

40
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:23,421
You can't get more than that.

41
00:02:23,541 --> 00:02:35,341
If you start winding on top, then because you wound on top, the magnetic field doesn't transfer well at high frequency to the second layer of turns.

42
00:02:35,341 --> 00:02:39,341
So that's just a pattern with any of these things.

43
00:02:40,121 --> 00:02:41,521
Take a bigger core.

44
00:02:41,621 --> 00:02:42,401
Well I did take one.

45
00:02:42,581 --> 00:02:42,921
So what?

46
00:02:43,381 --> 00:02:44,081
Nothing good.

47
00:02:44,621 --> 00:02:48,841
That's why the L3 coil is wound along the whole length.

48
00:02:50,041 --> 00:02:51,801
The more turns you can fit, the better.

49
00:02:51,941 --> 00:02:52,741
But I'll say it again.

50
00:02:53,221 --> 00:02:59,021
Because of the PVC, you could probably use thinner wire here and wind more turns.

51
00:02:59,181 --> 00:03:00,421
Yes, the voltage would go up.

52
00:03:00,421 --> 00:03:06,601
But it still won't light up four LEDs, so I had to use a second chip as an inverter.

53
00:03:07,201 --> 00:03:11,561
So this is a flyback inverter, 14 turns of wire.

54
00:03:12,381 --> 00:03:14,681
It can put out pretty much any voltage here.

55
00:03:15,901 --> 00:03:16,841
You see what the deal is?

56
00:03:17,141 --> 00:03:18,621
So say I need 60 volts.

57
00:03:18,681 --> 00:03:22,721
I can easily pull 60 volts out of this flyback.

58
00:03:22,721 --> 00:03:30,821
And at these frequencies, the ferrite doesn't "see" anything going on.

59
00:03:31,381 --> 00:03:32,561
It doesn't remagnetize.

60
00:03:32,701 --> 00:03:35,961
Especially considering that this generator is running.

61
00:03:36,761 --> 00:03:37,741
That's all, folks.

62
00:03:39,121 --> 00:03:40,781
The frequency of this ferrite, here it is.

63
00:03:40,881 --> 00:03:41,861
67.53.

64
00:03:42,361 --> 00:03:42,501
Right?

65
00:03:42,961 --> 00:03:44,221
And 2% duty cycle.

66
00:03:45,581 --> 00:03:46,241
There you go.

67
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:48,841
So, like...

68
00:03:48,841 --> 00:03:51,121
Look, watch, I'll disconnect it now, everything will go out.

69
00:03:51,121 --> 00:03:51,841
There.

70
00:03:52,361 --> 00:03:52,921
That's it.

71
00:03:53,261 --> 00:03:53,581
See that?

72
00:03:54,321 --> 00:03:54,581
There.

73
00:03:56,161 --> 00:03:57,281
Connecting it back.

74
00:03:57,381 --> 00:04:00,121
Everything, just like on the oscilloscope.

75
00:04:01,021 --> 00:04:01,901
That's the picture.

76
00:04:04,881 --> 00:04:07,021
Well, it's all pretty basic, damn.

77
00:04:07,121 --> 00:04:08,121
Nothing special.

78
00:04:08,561 --> 00:04:10,881
And that's how it's done.

79
00:04:12,181 --> 00:04:13,001
I don't mind sharing it.

80
00:04:13,121 --> 00:04:14,001
Go ahead, build it.

81
00:04:14,101 --> 00:04:17,121
I've kind of studied this topic, but I know that this flashlight...

82
00:04:17,121 --> 00:04:18,661
Well, I mean...

83
00:04:20,641 --> 00:04:22,421
This is my own design.

84
00:04:22,641 --> 00:04:25,321
This isn't the one Akula had with two generators.

85
00:04:25,421 --> 00:04:30,901
The one where he was posting these schematics all over the internet.

86
00:04:31,161 --> 00:04:34,141
Like, he supposedly put in this...

87
00:04:34,141 --> 00:04:36,061
It was supposedly better and all that.

88
00:04:37,841 --> 00:04:42,201
I don't know what he was going for, working with something like that.

89
00:04:42,281 --> 00:04:44,021
I actually built this generator, by the way.

90
00:04:44,021 --> 00:04:45,381
I never did figure out what...

91
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:48,201
he'd hooked up wrong here, or where.

92
00:04:48,821 --> 00:04:50,081
And why exactly like that.

93
00:04:51,101 --> 00:04:54,061
But this generator of mine, yeah, it worked for me, that's it.

94
00:04:54,281 --> 00:04:56,101
But how do you tune it?

95
00:04:56,701 --> 00:04:59,241
With a 0.22 nF trimmer capacitor.

96
00:05:00,001 --> 00:05:01,761
Makes you wonder, what kind of capacitor is that anyway?

97
00:05:03,081 --> 00:05:04,201
To dial in the frequency?

98
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:06,061
Beats me.

99
00:05:07,021 --> 00:05:11,301
Honestly, I think all these schematics are insanely far-fetched.

100
00:05:11,401 --> 00:05:13,101
I mean, they just can't work.

101
00:05:13,101 --> 00:05:15,881
Most likely, this particular circuit was actually a working one.

102
00:05:17,001 --> 00:05:23,301
But here the transformer also uses magnetostriction resonance.

103
00:05:24,921 --> 00:05:29,461
One of the coils, most likely, is using this magnetostriction resonance.

104
00:05:30,061 --> 00:05:30,941
Why do I think that?

105
00:05:31,061 --> 00:05:32,101
Because...

106
00:05:32,661 --> 00:05:35,141
Well, the schematic's wrong, but...

107
00:05:36,761 --> 00:05:39,301
There's something missing from the drawing here.

108
00:05:41,141 --> 00:05:45,601
Specifically, plates that aren't drawn in on both sides, to create a capacitor right inside the coil.

109
00:05:46,461 --> 00:05:49,501
So that the coil would charge up and go into resonance from magnetostriction.

110
00:05:50,241 --> 00:05:54,481
Basically, that's what I wanted to implement here, in this system.

111
00:05:55,761 --> 00:05:56,401
But...

112
00:05:56,401 --> 00:06:01,621
It worked without it too, so I never really took it any further.

113
00:06:02,061 --> 00:06:05,381
I also tried making magnetostriction happen on something else.

114
00:06:05,641 --> 00:06:08,081
On this coil right here.

115
00:06:09,301 --> 00:06:12,581
I managed to get it to work on it once, so I tried again.

116
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:16,221
See, here I was rewinding it, checking how the ferrite behaves.

117
00:06:16,461 --> 00:06:18,181
So anyway, don't pay attention to that.

118
00:06:18,341 --> 00:06:19,981
I mean, this isn't wound the right way.

119
00:06:20,701 --> 00:06:20,981
There.

120
00:06:21,241 --> 00:06:26,861
Then, long story short, I made two plates and tried to get it into resonance.

121
00:06:26,981 --> 00:06:28,001
Well, didn't work out.

122
00:06:28,941 --> 00:06:31,361
Nothing good came of it, so to speak.

123
00:06:31,501 --> 00:06:33,781
It just didn't want to work, wouldn't cooperate.

124
00:06:33,901 --> 00:06:36,081
So, like...

125
00:06:36,081 --> 00:06:37,161
And forget about it.

126
00:06:37,801 --> 00:06:38,101
Right.

127
00:06:38,101 --> 00:06:41,081
As for this ferrite, I'll say it again.

128
00:06:41,581 --> 00:06:42,621
Well, it just doesn't work.

129
00:06:43,501 --> 00:06:44,381
Doesn't work.

130
00:06:45,181 --> 00:06:48,641
I mean, sure, it shows these nice-looking spikes and everything.

131
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,221
Here, by the way, these spikes, there they are.

132
00:06:50,821 --> 00:06:54,401
They've got a pretty big, um...

133
